    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim that the driver cancelled on you is not supported by the records. The no-show charge tests the driver's conduct, and on the platform's telemetry he met every condition. His trace places him inside the Changi T3 Door 5 pickup geofence from 22:40:00, 24 m from the pin — well within the 150 m airport arrival radius — and he tapped 'arrived' at 22:40:20. He then held position without moving for 500 seconds, 20 seconds more than the 480 seconds an airport pickup requires, and cancelled at 22:48:20 citing RIDER_NO_SHOW. Your own device sat about 519 m from the pin, outside the 200 m airport presence radius, so the rider-contact clause (POL-NS-04) cannot excuse the fee in any event: you messaged at 22:41:40, but the driver replied 18 seconds later, inside the 120-second window that clause allows. Because the waiting period was served in full, POL-NS-06 gives you no refund, and the fare breakdown reconciles at SGD 6.00 against the fee schedule (the AIRPORT zone fee and the RYDE_PLUS tier fee are both 6.00, so the greater is 6.00) — no fare defect under POL-NS-08(d). To the driver: the fee stands and you are compensated. All four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold on the telemetry, no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the charge, and POL-NS-03 is not engaged because your stationary fixes were inside the arrival radius rather than outside it. Under POL-NS-07 you receive 80 percent of the fee, SGD 4.80. The anti-farming check does not bite: 1 no-show termination in 30 days against 120 completed trips is below both limbs. The only artifact below full weight is the missing traffic advisory at weight 0.0, which carries no fact and which no finding rests on; the deciding artifacts — trip record, GPS trace, fare breakdown and driver profile — are all at weight 1.0, so the ruling is not discounted and the case is not escalated. Two of the driver's claims were discarded by the referee for citing the missing advisory without naming its